<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61553" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λᾰγών</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όνος</span>, ἡ, also ὁ, <i><span class="en">
			Hp.
			<u>Int.</u>
			25
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Aret.
			<u>SD</u>
			2.11
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαγαρός</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the hollow on each side below the
				ribs, flank</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				119
			</span></i>&lt;*&gt;, <i><span class="en">
				Chaerem.
				14.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				493a18
			</span></i>, al.: freq. in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαγόνες</span>,
				<i>flanks</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Batr.
				222
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				298
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				662
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαγόνων ὀστᾶ</span>
			<i>iliac</i> bones, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				2.507
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				772
			</span></i>; prop. of men, but also of animals, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				826
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				4.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.246
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύννου λαγόνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					132.5
				</span></i>
			 (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> pl.,
			in later Greek, <i>womb</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Naumach.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.22.32
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύσις αἰνίγματος</span> ap.Arg.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph., any
			<i>hollow</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοίλη λ.</span>
			<i>hollow</i> of a cup, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				43
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαγόνεσσι φαρέτρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.326
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινι λ. τοῦ κρημνοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Arat.</u>
					22
				</span></i>
			; esp. of a mountain, <i>flank</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				3.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cleom.
				1.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				185
			</span></i> (pl.); <i>bank</i> of a river, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαιᾷ ποταμοῦ . . λαγόνι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.287
				</span></i>
			 (Antip.); <i>sides</i> of a grave, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.2001
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθόνιαι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				7.117
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Megara</span>).</div>
